        {
          "id": "schedule-section-4",
          "type": "story_block",
          "intent": "A moment of deliberate stillness in a functional page \u2014 explain the philosophy behind the schedule structure so the visitor understands that session timing and frequency are not arbitrary but are built around proven acquisition science.",
          "eyebrow": "Why the Schedule Is Built This Way",
          "headline": "Frequency Is the Mechanism. Not Motivation.",
          "subheadline": null,
          "body": "Language acquisition research is unambiguous: distributed practice beats marathon sessions. BRUTALK's schedule is built around two 90-minute live sessions per week \u2014 enough frequency to maintain active recall, short enough to demand full presence every time. We don't offer daily classes because daily classes produce fatigue, not fluency. We don't offer weekly classes because one session a week produces forgetting, not progress. Two sessions. Ninety minutes each. Every week. That's the dose.",
